  "notes": "AST/dataflow rule: intraprocedural const/taint propagation catches VARIABLE-MEDIATED injection the line-oriented regex rules provably miss (a dangerous value assembled in one statement, used in a later statement). Sinks: eval/new Function (ast-eval-injection, high), child_process exec/execSync + spawn(shell:true) (ast-command-injection, critical), .query/.execute/.raw with a dynamic SQL-shaped non-parameterized arg (ast-sql-injection, high). fpMode any — ANY finding on a negative is an FP. The hard FP guard is const-propagation: a variable bound only to constant strings is CONST-SAFE and never flagged (incl. the prototype's `const q=`SELECT 1`; db.query(q)` FP). Conservative by design: bare unknown identifiers, cross-function flow, and non-SQL .query() do NOT flag. Positives are SYNTHETIC (honest).",
